Ben,

Thanks for the insights!

[finance details] I actually lived out of my car for the past couple =
years so I was able to keep expenses mostly low. I=E2=80=99ve traveled a =
crazy amount though so savings are still at $0 (actually negative with =
loan and credit debt). Average last three months from mint.com =
<http://mint.com/>, 400 for food, 300 for gas/car, 300 for loans, and =
120 for phone.=20

I finished the book today and I really like the idea of working in oil =
or with the defense contractors for a year or two just to pay off all my =
debt and save some money. I was already looking to get into oil abroad =
with the chemical engineering degree. Ideally, my goal is to end up =
living in Russia but I=E2=80=99m willing to sacrifice location for a =
year in order to get my finances back on the right foot. I=E2=80=99m =
open to relocating anywhere if the opportunity is good.=20

That said, I plan on spreading my applications far and wide and choosing =
the best option as you suggested. I attached my resume which I have =
already slightly modified for teaching. I highlighted the few bullets =
that were related to teaching e.g. training employees in safety or =
soccer coaching. Not sure how to reframe these other bullets for =
teaching but let me know if you have any other ideas or thoughts. If I =
should be looking for double, I=E2=80=99ll go ahead and reject this =
offer and apply for better options.=20

I look forward to your response!

Best,

Chibuzor (Chi) Ejimofor
