normal; letter-spacing: normal; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; =
text-transform: none; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; =
-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration: none;" class=3D"">Hi, =
Chi!<span class=3D"Apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span><br class=3D""><br =
class=3D"">Welcome aboard! It's great to hear from you.<span =
class=3D"Apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span><br class=3D""><br =
class=3D"">You have a bachelor's degree, are in the process of getting =
your TEFL, and have a top-notch passport. These will go a long way =
abroad.<span class=3D"Apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span><br =
class=3D""><br class=3D"">Given that you rank money as a top priority, I =
would encourage you not to walk away from this contract... but to =
actually run away from it. This is very, very low. You can do much, much =
better.<span class=3D"Apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span><br =
class=3D""><br class=3D"">One of the first things I would do is consider =
how much of that $80k salary you had left over each month after you paid =
all of your expenses. Once you have this baseline, we can look at how =
much would be required to match it. It's probably a lot lower than you =
think.&nbsp;</div></div></blockquote><blockquote type=3D"cite" =
class=3D""><div class=3D""><div dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"caret-color: rgb(0, =
0, 0); font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px; font-style: normal; =
font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; =
text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: =
normal; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; =
text-decoration: none;" class=3D""><br class=3D"">Matching a high salary =
in the countries you've specified is going to be rough. But it's =
entirely possible to do it somewhere like China.<span =
class=3D"Apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span><br class=3D""><br =
class=3D"">Generally speaking I encourage no one to ever work for less =
than 200 RMB or $30US per hour in China because it's just not necessary. =
I very rarely see training center contracts that pencil out. The best =
positions are in public and private K-12 and universities and colleges. =
Once you've worked your way through the manual, please let me know what =
you're thinking and we can go from there.<span =
class=3D"Apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span><br class=3D""><br =
class=3D"">Many people also find that they're not getting as many hits =
and as high quality of offers as they'd like because their resumes are =
off. You can upgrade your package if desired within the first 30 days =
and we can work on getting all of your documents looking professional =
and polished.<span class=3D"Apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span><br =
class=3D""><br class=3D"">Ideally I'd like to see you get at very least =
double what this contract is offering in terms of hourly compensation. I =
look forward to continuing this conversation with you.<span =
class=3D"Apple-converted-space">&nbsp;</span><br class=3D""><br =
class=3D"">Ben&nbsp;<br class=3D""><span class=3D""></span></div><br =
style=3D"caret-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Helvetica; font-size: =
